[statement]
A package installed rules out a candidate whose dependency on its name it
does not meet, where another package could: `python3` 3.14, installed for
`a`, rules out `py` r10, which needs `python3~3.12`, since `python3` 3.12
is offered too, and `py` r9 is installed. Contrast
`refusals/a-holder-does-not-rule-out-a-dependent-nothing-could-meet`.

[repository]
P:python3
V:3.14.10-r1

P:python3
V:3.12.1-r0

P:a
V:1
D:python3~3.14

P:py
V:1.1-r9

P:py
V:1.1-r10
D:python3~3.12

[request]
a
py

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install python3 3.14.10-r1
install a 1
install py 1.1-r9
